01:09:09.100 --> 01:09:11.930
But yeah, if you want to do
kind of mass transformations,

01:09:11.930 --> 01:09:15.180
you should use whatever tools
you are comfortable with.

01:09:15.180 --> 01:09:17.220
If you want to stay
within Google Cloud,

01:09:17.220 --> 01:09:20.819
you can run that
Spark on Dataproc.

01:09:20.819 --> 01:09:23.229
And if you're kind of
developing a new set of ETL,

01:09:23.229 --> 01:09:27.569
you can also use things
like a Beam on Dataflow.

01:09:27.569 --> 01:09:32.460
So Beam is an Apache open source
kind of ETL transformation tool

01:09:32.460 --> 01:09:36.930
that allows you to use the
same source code to transform

01:09:36.930 --> 01:09:39.834
both stream and batch data.

01:09:39.834 --> 01:09:41.250
That's where the
name comes from--

01:09:41.250 --> 01:09:43.109
Beam is batch and stream.

01:09:43.109 --> 01:09:46.290
And you can run it
on Dataflow, which

01:09:46.290 --> 01:09:49.979
is intended to be kind of a
next generation ETL service

01:09:49.979 --> 01:09:52.519
where you can just, basically--
it's sort of like the way

01:09:52.519 --> 01:09:54.810
a [INAUDIBLE] works where
you can just submit your code

01:09:54.810 --> 01:09:55.760
and it will just run.

01:09:55.760 --> 01:09:57.090
You don't have to
think about machines,

01:09:57.090 --> 01:09:59.256
and the size of the machines,
and how many machines.

01:09:59.256 --> 01:10:02.220
It's just, here's my Beam
code, here's my data,

01:10:02.220 --> 01:10:03.190
go make it happen.

01:10:03.190 --> 01:10:05.220
And it paralyzes
everything for you.

01:10:05.220 --> 01:10:07.230
So that part of it's nice.

01:10:07.230 --> 01:10:10.770
The final piece of it
would be tf.Transform,

01:10:10.770 --> 01:10:12.710
which is a library
for doing-- you

01:10:12.710 --> 01:10:14.790
guessed it-- transformations.

01:10:14.790 --> 01:10:16.929
It's based on the
Beam API so there's

01:10:16.929 --> 01:10:18.720
a lot of similarities
there which allow you

01:10:18.720 --> 01:10:21.790
to kind of carry things over.

01:10:21.790 --> 01:10:25.470
But by and large,
those would be some

01:10:25.470 --> 01:10:28.180
