01:12:35.299 --> 01:12:37.640
PUNEITH KAUL: Yeah,
so basically Keras

01:12:37.640 --> 01:12:41.470
is the official TensorFlow
model authoring layer.

01:12:41.470 --> 01:12:44.570
So you want to use Keras to
author your architecture.

01:12:44.570 --> 01:12:47.030
The dispatch and the
execution of the model

01:12:47.030 --> 01:12:50.856
itself should be done
through estimate API.

01:12:50.856 --> 01:12:52.980
What that means is that
your authoring language now

01:12:52.980 --> 01:12:57.590
is much less verbose, and
it has all the same benefits

01:12:57.590 --> 01:13:01.070
of TensorFlow, because
the underlying execution

01:13:01.070 --> 01:13:03.050
engine is actually TensorFlow.

01:13:03.050 --> 01:13:06.180
So that was actually an
official thing from TensorFlow,

01:13:06.180 --> 01:13:08.540
and that's why you
want to use a df Keras,

01:13:08.540 --> 01:13:13.550
because it subsumes
the open source Keras.

01:13:13.550 --> 01:13:16.490
YUFENG GUO: And the
rationale behind

01:13:16.490 --> 01:13:20.270
why we recommend converting
to estimator in general,

01:13:20.270 --> 01:13:22.192
and training on the
estimator-- it's

01:13:22.192 --> 01:13:23.650
like, I already
have a Keras model,

01:13:23.650 --> 01:13:25.580
why don't I just
